clearcote: bit-exact Windows UCRT tanh for a Windows persona.

Math.tanh is the only Math.* that reads the host libm -- V8 bundles the rest, but since Chrome 148
ieee754::tanh delegates to std::tanh. A Windows persona on a Linux host therefore returns glibc bits
where real Windows Chrome returns UCRT bits. Measured on our own builds, identical persona and UA:

    tanh(0.7)   win 3fe356fb17af2e91   linux 3fe356fb17af2e92    1 ULP
    tanh(0.8)   win 3fe53fca0a748a40   linux 3fe53fca0a748a42    2 ULP
    tanh(0.9)   win 3fe6ebe982d6605c   linux 3fe6ebe982d6605d    1 ULP

One call on the right input classifies the host OS, needing no reference data and no population
baseline. Returning a third value (fdlibm, or noise) does not fix it: every browser since 148
returns its host's bits, so a neutral value matches no real OS and becomes its own anomaly. The only
correct output is exactly what the CLAIMED OS produces.

The UCRT reproduction (tables, exp kernel, rational cores) is from arman-bd/chromiumfish, MIT,
commit 004a4f51 -- a reverse engineering of ucrtbase.dll tanh. It uses only fma() and IEEE-754
primitives, so it is architecture-neutral and no Microsoft binary is redistributed.

Two deliberate differences from that original, both about which way to fail:
  * it defaults to the Windows kernel when the persona switch is absent or unreadable; we default to
    the HOST libm. Our containers run a Linux persona by default, where glibc is the honest answer,
    so defaulting to Windows would invent a contradiction on the common configuration.
  * every failure path -- no /proc, short read, unparseable value -- also falls through to std::tanh.

Installed at base::ieee754::tanh, the single chokepoint shared by the runtime lowering AND TurboFan
constant folding. Patching only one would make the value CHANGE as a function tiers up: a page can
loop until JIT promotion and watch it flip, which is a louder tell than the original.

The persona is read from /proc/self/cmdline rather than base::CommandLine because V8 must build
standalone and cannot depend on components/ungoogled. The result is cached keyed on getpid() so it
is re-read after the zygote fork -- a magic static would initialise in the zygote, whose command
line carries no persona switch, and every renderer would inherit that answer.

Verified on the built Linux binary against genuine UCRT bits captured from our own Windows build on
real Windows hardware: the windows persona matches on 8/8 inputs including the 2-ULP case, the linux
persona still returns glibc on the 3 inputs that differ, and every other Math.* is bit-identical.

